y hard  for me to stay awake you don't really  have that same problem in a racecar  thankfully you could say I've never  heard of someone falling asleep at the  wheel when you're actually going at it  things just happen too quickly but that  can sometimes give you a false sense of  security that just because you can keep  your eyes open that your mind is open to  and that you're making all the  adjustments to your routine as  circumstances demand them because  driving around a racetrack for 24 hours  it means that the track changes you have  all sorts of things people go off track  people were not dude they pull on gravel  onto the track you have to make constant  alterations so you have to not just be a  weight but be have an open mind to  changing things and changing things up  and I think that is probably one of the  hardest things for a lot of drivers that  just keeping in that open mode not just  putting it on autopilot because they're  not a pilot that's when you make a  mistake and the next time you come  around for some corner there's a car  that's tracked something onto the track  or the track itself just changes over  the 24 hours it changes immensely more  Robert goes down or if you have whether  any of these other things so that's some  of the considerations I put into it that  is why I think Lamont is the greatest  race in the world because it brings  these challenges you don't usually feel  when you do a six hour racer or 45  minute race for that matter it's a  unique challenge to make no mistakes and  stay on your game for 24 hours  Stuart Howard Smith's asks where do you  take a piss when racing a 24 hour a limo  race well in the seat that's is the  honest truth I have never in my six  years of racing hat to pee that bad and  I went in my seat but I guarantee you  that had lots and lots of drivers have I  was just actually in the ten hour race  in the u.s. a couple months ago and my  co-driver got damn peed in the seat and  he was in the start of his stint he's  been out for an hour and I think the  realization that he had to be in the car  for another two  half-hours he just went [ __ ] it I'm  peeing in my seat and of course the team  is laughing and laughing and laughing  and why are they laughing well they  don't have to go into the seat after him  I had to go into the seat after him and  the guy one of the mechanics would go oh  you're gonna have such a monkey but when  you get out because apparently when you  sit in other people's pee for a couple  of hours like that's not that great for  your skin it soaks in through your suit  and well Channel is just disgusting I  think that that is one of the drawbacks  of team racing when you have multiple  drivers in the lineup who have to share  a car together well it's more than the  other guys if you pee in your seat at  least if you pee it's your own pee so  people simply just go it doesn't happen  all the time it doesn't happen  frequently but it does happen often  enough that absolutely the consequences  is something that most race teams have  been a business for a while they know  all about hey guys this is Tim again  just a few more things before you take  off number one this is five bullet  Friday do you want to get a short email  from me and would you enjoy getting a  short email for me every Friday is that  provides a little morsel of fun before  the weekend and five bullet Friday is a  very short email where I share the  coolest things I've found or that I've  been pondering over the week that could  include favourite new albums that I've  discovered it could include gizmos and  gadgets and all sorts of weird [ __ ] that  I've somehow dug up in the the world of  the esoteric as I do  it could include favorite articles that  I have read and that I've shared with my  close friends for instance and it's very  short it's just a little tiny bite of  goodness before you head off for the  weekend so if you want to receive that  check it out just go to 4-hour wo